#
# Code owners of the paths that decide whether a history rewrite can be merged.
# Copy this file to .github/CODEOWNERS and replace OWNER-LOGIN with the login of
# the review account (README.md, "History rewrites", "Who reviews when you are
# the only person"). A code owner must have write access to the repository.
#
# This file does nothing by itself. It is the primary boundary only together
# with the branch rule "Require review from Code Owners", an owner who is not
# the pull request author, "Dismiss stale pull request approvals" on,
# "Require approval of the most recent reviewable push" on, and administrators
# included in the rules (no bypass). Follow the activation checklist in the
# README before you add an approver login.
#
# GitHub reads this file from the base branch of the pull request, so a pull
# request cannot change who owns a path for itself.
#
# Note: /history/ is also changed by the daily refresh pull requests. With the
# code-owner rule on, those need the same review, so choose how you want to
# handle them before you turn the rule on.

/.github/                       @OWNER-LOGIN
/.github/history-approvers      @OWNER-LOGIN
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @OWNER-LOGIN
/.github/workflows/             @OWNER-LOGIN
/history/                       @OWNER-LOGIN
/scripts/                       @OWNER-LOGIN
/engine.lock                    @OWNER-LOGIN
/engine.release.json            @OWNER-LOGIN
